From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:16:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: turned hubs with end-face outlines, mixed-family and
 longer goals, revolves off the origin

- ext/mixed.py: split "turned" (a hub turned about X, Y or Z, optionally bored and away
  from the origin; a curved blade, curved slot or other outline on its end face, polar-patterned
  about the axis; optional axial bore or bolt circle) and split "mixed" (a box base with
  several feature groups from different families on different regions: top features, rows
  and mirrors, side-face features, rows, windows and mirrors, cross bores; 3-11 intents at
  level 3, 8-14 at level 4). Neither produces a held-out composition.
- Revolve goals: 35 % of the profiles away from the origin along the axis (0.3-3 x scale).
- Training: mixed drawn 3x as often as the other expanded splits; level-1 training goals
  include lone outline, revolve and turned bases (half the expanded fraction), so the model
  learns to stop right after such a base.
- Suites turned, mixed, mixed_long (level 4, longer than training).
- python -m freecad_s1.ext.mixed writes sampled goals to a goals JSON (for a teacher check).
